/*
 * Bitcoin and the S&P 500, daily, from FRED.
 *
 * CBBTCUSD (Coinbase Bitcoin) and SP500. Pulled 2026-09-22. FRED keeps
 * only the last ten years of SP500, which is why the two series start on
 * different days; anything comparing them uses the overlap.
 *
 * Bitcoin trades every day, so its closes are one per calendar day from
 * BTC.start, with the handful of days FRED has no observation for carried
 * forward from the day before. The S&P trades on business days, so its closes
 * carry their own offsets from SPX.start in days, and holidays are absent
 * rather than invented.
 *
 * Refresh with the S&P file (see ../Timing/spxData.ts), twice a year:
 *   curl -s "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/graph/fredgraph.csv?id=CBBTCUSD"
 *   curl -s "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/graph/fredgraph.csv?id=SP500"
 */

